        {
          "file": "research/numerical-optimization-dynamics-2026-10-16-batch-91.proof-contracts.json",
          "id": "alg-improved-tangent-climbing-neb",
          "field": "evidence",
          "case": "zero",
          "literal_source_excerpt": true,
          "value": "Definition: the climbing image has no spring force. The remaining interior images retain the ordinary force. Thus iterations $k=0,\\ldots,n_{\\rm climb}-1$ use ordinary forces and the first climbing force is evaluated at iteration $k=n_{\\rm climb}$. At each iteration report the maximum force norm and spacing residual $\\max_i|\\|\\Delta_i^+\\|_2-\\|\\Delta_i^-\\|_2|$. Stop with `tolerances-met` only if both are within their declared tolerances. If a tolerance fails and $k=N$, return `budget-exhausted`; only when $k<N$ update every interior image by $R_i^{k+1}=R_i^k+\\eta F_i^k$. Leaving $U$ returns `geometry-failure`. After a valid update set $k\\leftarrow k+1$ and repeat. The tolerance check precedes the budget check, so $N=0$ still checks the initial chain and $n_{\\rm climb}=N$ uses a climbing force at the final residual check (without an update if the budget is then exhausted).",
          "disposition": "exact source excerpt"
        }
